-- title:
--   Corollary 25 — the set $Q$ of two-sided admissible updates is convex, symmetric and has volume $\ge2^{-5m}$ (corrected: $0<\varepsilon\le1$)
-- statement:
--   There is a universal constant $c_0>0$ such that the following holds. Let $Z\subseteq\mathbb R^n$ be the zonotope generated by the rows of $A\in\mathbb R^{m\times n}$, let $0<\varepsilon\le1$ and $m\ge c_0n/\varepsilon^2$. Then the set
--   $$Q=\big\{x\in[-1,1]^m:\ (1-\varepsilon)Z\subseteq Z_{\mathbf1+x}\subseteq(1+\varepsilon)Z\big\}$$
--   1. is convex;
--   2. is symmetric, $Q=-Q$;
--   3. has volume $\mathrm{Vol}_m(Q)\ge2^{-5m}$.
--
--   $Q$ is the set of row rescalings that keep the zonotope within a factor $1\pm\varepsilon$; combined with a partial-coloring argument it drives the iterative sparsification that proves Theorem 1.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - correction: ε > 0 → 0 < ε ≤ 1; reason: for ε > 1 symmetry fails: n = 1, ε = 3/2, m ≥ max(1, 4c₀/9) rows all equal to 1 give Z = [−m,m] and Q = {x ∈ [−1,1]^m : Σx_i ≥ −m/2}, which contains 𝟏 but not −𝟏; every printed assumption holds. ε ≤ 1 covers Theorem 1's whole range
--   - encoding: c₀ > 0 a universal constant → ∃ c₀ > 0 quantified before m, n, A, ε; reason: the meaning of 'universal'
--   - encoding: Q symmetric → ∀ x ∈ Q, −x ∈ Q; reason: origin symmetry
--   - encoding: Lebesgue volume Vol (a value in [0,∞]) → (volume ·).toReal; reason: every set measured here is bounded, so its volume is finite and toReal is the same number
-- source:
--   Victor Reis, Thomas Rothvoss, Linear-size ℓ1 sparsifiers, STOC 2027 submission #162 (October 2026; PDF SHA-256 5137e7dee3cd303bd508f90f5f42c955632af5dc2ec978d9ef575bae4ce23710), §6, Corollary 25, pp.15–16

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_L1Sparsifiers_Main_Zonotope
import Definitions.Def_L1Sparsifiers_Main_UniformCube

namespace L1Sparsifiers.Main

open MeasureTheory
open scoped Pointwise

/-- **Corollary 25** (pp.15–16), with the accuracy range corrected to `0 < ε ≤ 1`.
"There is a universal constant c₀ > 0 so that the following holds: Let Z ⊆ ℝⁿ be a zonotope
generated by the rows of A ∈ ℝ^{m×n}. For ε > 0 and m ≥ c₀n/ε² the set
Q = {x ∈ [−1,1]^m | (1−ε)Z ⊆ Z_{1+x} ⊆ (1+ε)Z} is convex and symmetric, and has volume
Vol_m(Q) ≥ 2^{−5m}."

`c₀` is chosen before `m, n, A, ε`; symmetric means `Q = −Q`. -/
theorem corollary_25 :
    ∃ c₀ : ℝ, 0 < c₀ ∧
      ∀ {m n : ℕ} (A : Matrix (Fin m) (Fin n) ℝ) (ε : ℝ), 0 < ε → ε ≤ 1 → c₀ * n / ε ^ 2 ≤ m →
        Convex ℝ {x ∈ cube m | (1 - ε) • zonotope A 1 ⊆ zonotope A (1 + x) ∧
            zonotope A (1 + x) ⊆ (1 + ε) • zonotope A 1} ∧
          (∀ x ∈ {x ∈ cube m | (1 - ε) • zonotope A 1 ⊆ zonotope A (1 + x) ∧
              zonotope A (1 + x) ⊆ (1 + ε) • zonotope A 1},
            -x ∈ {x ∈ cube m | (1 - ε) • zonotope A 1 ⊆ zonotope A (1 + x) ∧
              zonotope A (1 + x) ⊆ (1 + ε) • zonotope A 1}) ∧
          ((2 : ℝ) ^ (5 * m))⁻¹ ≤
            (volume {x ∈ cube m | (1 - ε) • zonotope A 1 ⊆ zonotope A (1 + x) ∧
              zonotope A (1 + x) ⊆ (1 + ε) • zonotope A 1}).toReal := by sorry

end L1Sparsifiers.Main
